---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

import ArchitectureField from "../components/ArchitectureField.astro";
import ExpandableProjectCard from "../components/ExpandableProjectCard.astro";
import ExperienceLog from "../components/ExperienceLog.astro";
import GovernanceChecklist from "../components/GovernanceChecklist.astro";
import IdentityBlock from "../components/IdentityBlock.astro";
import StackManifest from "../components/StackManifest.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Farnaz Zinnah — AI Systems Engineer"
  description="AI Systems Engineer working across AI infrastructure, distributed systems, adversarial machine learning, and AI governance."
>
  <main
    id="main"
    class="mx-auto max-w-6xl space-y-24 px-6 pt-10 pb-28 md:pt-14 lg:pr-12 lg:pb-20"
  >
    <!-- HERO -->
    <section
      class="relative isolate grid min-h-[55vh] items-center gap-12 overflow-hidden py-8 md:grid-cols-2"
      aria-labelledby="hero-title"
    >
      <ArchitectureField />

      <div class="relative z-10 space-y-5">
        <p
          class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-cyan"
        >
          AI Systems · Security · Infrastructure
        </p>

        <h1
          id="hero-title"
          class="text-4xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight md:text-5xl"
        >
          Farnaz Zinnah
        </h1>

        <p class="max-w-md text-lg leading-8 text-paper/80">
          I build AI systems, break them on purpose to see how they fail, and
          help decide which ones are actually safe to ship.
        </p>

        <button
          type="button"
          data-scroll-target="work"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-accent-cyan/50 px-4 py-2.5 font-mono text-sm text-accent-cyan transition-colors hover:border-accent-cyan hover:bg-accent-cyan/5"
        >
          See selected work
          <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="relative z-10">
        <IdentityBlock />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- EXPERIENCE + STACK -->
    <section
      class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2"
      aria-label="Experience and technical stack"
    >
      <div id="experience" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="border-b border-paper/10 pb-2 text-2xl font-semibold">
          Experience
        </h2>

        <p class="text-sm text-paper/60">
          Mostly Con Edison so far, with school running alongside it.
        </p>

        <ExperienceLog />
      </div>

      <div id="stack" class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-3">
        <h2 class="border-b border-paper/10 pb-2 text-2xl font-semibold">
          Stack
        </h2>

        <p class="text-sm text-paper/60">
          Not everything here makes it onto a resume bullet.
        </p>

        <StackManifest />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SELECTED WORK -->
    <section
      id="work"
      class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6"
      aria-labelledby="work-title"
    >
      <h2
        id="work-title"
        class="border-b border-paper/10 pb-2 text-2xl font-semibold"
      >
        Selected Work
      </h2>

      <p class="text-sm text-paper/70">
        Most of my day-to-day work lives in private enterprise repos. These are
        the ones I can actually show.
      </p>

      <div class="grid items-start gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <ExpandableProjectCard
          size="large"
          title="Adversarial Robustness Testing"
          hook="Fooled a production image classifier down to 0.2% accuracy with changes you can't see."
          details="I wanted to know how easily a production-grade image classifier could be fooled. Turns out: very. A PGD attack dropped accuracy from 76% to 0.2%, and the trick transferred to a completely different model 90% of the time. Measured on a held-out ImageNet-1K validation subset, PGD run at ε=8/255, 20 steps. Built solo in PyTorch. Happy to walk through the exact setup if asked."
          stack={["PyTorch", "ImageNet-1K", "Security"]}
          href="https://github.com/fzinnah17/neural-network-jailbreak"
        />

        <ExpandableProjectCard
          title="Mojo vs CUDA"
          hook="Mojo's compiler kernels against a decade of CUDA optimization: closer than I expected."
          details="Mojo is still young, so I wanted to see how its compiler-generated GPU kernels stack up against CUDA's. On compute-heavy operations, Mojo won by 1.7–1.9x. On memory-bound ones, CUDA still had the edge. Co-built for HPML coursework."
          stack={["Mojo", "CUDA", "MAX Graph"]}
        />

        <ExpandableProjectCard
          title="Call Analytics Pipeline"
          hook="Cut manager review time from 6 hours to 1 hour per 100 calls."
          details="Managers were spending 6 hours reviewing 100 customer service calls by hand. I built a speech-to-text + LLM pipeline that got it down to 1 hour, with nothing persisting after processing."
          stack={["Azure Whisper", "GPT-4", "Python"]}
        />

        <ExpandableProjectCard
          title="Cloud-to-On-Prem Gateway"
          hook="The old system topped out at 25 endpoints. This one doesn't."
          details="The previous method for connecting cloud apps to on-prem systems topped out at 25 endpoints. I built a code-based relay that routes to as many destinations as needed, handles 1M+ requests a day, and stores routing rules separately so new routes can be added without touching application code."
          stack={["C#/.NET", "Azure Relay", "Table Storage"]}
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- GOVERNANCE -->
    <section
      id="governance"
      class="scroll-mt-24 space-y-6"
      aria-labelledby="governance-title"
    >
      <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-3">
        <p
          class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-cyan"
        >
          Architecture &amp; Governance
        </p>

        <h2 id="governance-title" class="text-2xl font-semibold">
          The other side of the table.
        </h2>

        <p class="leading-8 text-paper/80">
          Before an AI or automation system ships, someone has to actually look
          at it and ask if it's safe. That's part of my job too. It's slower and
          less flashy than the projects above, but it's the one I'd probably
          miss most if it went away.
        </p>
      </div>

      <GovernanceChecklist />

      <p class="text-sm leading-7 text-paper/70">
        Security by default shows up in the code above too, not just the review
        process: in-memory processing with no persistence, path-traversal
        validation, IP-restricted keys.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- OTHER WORK -->
    <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="other-work-title">
      <h2
        id="other-work-title"
        class="border-b border-paper/10 pb-2 text-2xl font-semibold"
      >
        Other Work
      </h2>

      <p class="text-sm text-paper/60">A few other things, briefly.</p>

      <ul class="space-y-3 text-paper/80">
        <li>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent-cyan">
            SDLC automation
          </span>
          — A hackathon build: agents syncing SharePoint and Azure DevOps, drafting
          user stories, and answering questions over the backlog with RAG.
        </li>

        <li>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent-cyan">
            Infrastructure risk
          </span>
          — Drone footage plus weather data, fused into a risk score for infrastructure
          inspection. Built on GCP.
        </li>

        <li>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent-cyan">
            AI governance agent
          </span>
          — A smaller, automated cousin of the review process above, built on Gemini
          and Vertex AI.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- TEACHING -->
    <section
      class="border-y border-paper/10 py-10"
      aria-labelledby="mentorship-title"
    >
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
        <p
          class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-cyan"
        >
          Teaching &amp; Mentorship
        </p>

        <h2 id="mentorship-title" class="text-2xl font-semibold">
          Didn't expect this to stick.
        </h2>

        <p class="leading-8 text-paper/80">
          I signed up to teach data structures as a CodePath Tech Fellow mostly
          for the resume line. Ended up doing it four semesters straight, 50+
          students, 94 NPS. Still mentor for CUNY Tech Prep's AI Ethics program
          and show up for hackathons at HackMIT and Columbia DevFest when I can.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
